    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The SEBI Board consists of a Chairman appointed by the Central Government of India.",
        "Two members are nominated from amongst the officials of the Union Ministry of Finance.",
        "One member is nominated from amongst the officials of the Reserve Bank of India (RBI).",
        "Five other members are nominated by the Central Government, of whom at least three must be whole-time members."
